    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n768" root="اسك" body-key="A">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَسَكَهَا</span></b> , aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اَسِكَ</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَسْكٌ</span>, <i>He hit, hurt,</i> or
<i>wounded, her</i> (a woman's) <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِسْكَتَانِ</span>. (TA.) And
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُسِكَتْ</span> <i>She</i> (a woman) <i>was hurt,</i> or <i>wounded, in a
place not that of circumcision,</i> [i.e., <i>in her</i>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِسْكَتَانِ</span>,] <i>by the circumcising woman's missing the
proper place.</i> (Msb.) [See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَظْرق</span>.]

